{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>In the day</b> — I will not call to test You and not for naught, for I am in distress." "<b>And the meaning of כי תענני</b> (that You answer me) — that I may know true knowledge, that You will answer me, because there is none like You among the Elohim, O YHWH — as Moses' words: כה׳ אלהינו בכל קראינו אליו (like YHWH our Elohim in all our calling to Him)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 86, :notes {1 "Resolved כי in כי תענני as introducing the object clause of אדע ('that I may know'), following the syntactic flow of Ibn Ezra's paraphrase."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:09.934120690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}